I think Serge in Darkness' solution is particularly clever.  I had not
even thought to simply exit the dungeon with her.  It's still fairly
early in the game, and I'm feeling a little less wary about starting
anew.  She will exit the dungeon, though not ascended, far better
equipped and much richer than she entered.  That one's under serious
consideration.  As far as continuing on my adventure and simply
allowing her to die when the moment inevitably comes, I've thought
that one over-- And while it's not technically a cheat to be in
eXplore mode (as Kerio points out), it does make me a little sad she
wouldn't have any immortality in the high score table.

The idea of eXplore mode not being an explicit cheat is interesting,
because the moral issue for me is still there, even though I recognize
(as Eskimo and Janis point out) that she's most likely going to die
anyway, as well as how practically irrational it is-- Since, as David
mentions, I will still be playing the same game for all intents and
purposes.  But my qualms also have a bit of a metaphysical aspect,
since I'm seeing a bit of a "taint" to my game regardless of the fact
that I have no intention of taking advantage of the death prompt.

I appreciate everyone's input, and I'll post later what I've decided
to do.

Thanks, everyone!
